※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4470

※ Something reads what the loop comes to, so every way out of it has to give
※ something.  A `break` that hands nothing over is a way out with nothing to
※ give, and there is no value for the block after the loop to read down it.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let found: u8? = while §counting true:
        if true:
            break §counting
        break §counting 2u8
    found ?? 0u8
